SlopWorld on Fedora
==================

As your normal user, attach the packaged mod to native Linux RimWorld 1.6:

  RIMWORLD=/path/to/RimWorld/game
  slopworld mod install --game "$RIMWORLD"
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user enable --now slopd.service
  slopworld

The installer saves the game path and uses /usr/share/slopworld/SlopWorld.
Use --source DIR for another mod tree. Omit --game if RIMWORLD is exported
or the path is saved. Enable SlopWorld in the game's mod list.
After upgrading, run as your normal user:

  slopworld mod install
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user try-restart slopd.service

Before removing the package, run as your normal user:

  systemctl --user disable --now slopd.service
  slopworld mod uninstall

After removal, run systemctl --user daemon-reload.
Configuration, sessions, and saves are preserved.
A source installation's unit under ~/.config/systemd/user overrides the packaged
unit; remove it before enabling this one.
